  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The recto of each panel has a color illustration with text that is partially visible above or below the image (model is Chen Shi-zeng).  The eight panels ([16] p.) are glued together using Kenzo red paper tape. When the eight panels are folded out, they form an octagon. A letterpress presentation of Anne Waldman's poem, Makeup on Empty Space, is printed on the verso of the panels.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"15 deluxe copies with a video tape of the original performance on May 1, 1999 in Poestenkill and a reading of two poems on CD by the poet. 55 regular copies.  6 copies hors commerce for the artists. Silkscreen printing on Chinese paper by Frank Kicherer, Stuttgart. Letterpress printing on handmade paper of the Kaldewey Press. Red borders specially colored by Richard Tuttle. Bindings and boxes by Judi Conant of Vermont"--Colophon.</subfield>
